      <h2>Publications &amp; Presentations</h2>

      <p>
        My research spans remote sensing, hydrology, geomorphology,
        karst science, environmental microbiology, and geospatial analysis.
        This page highlights manuscripts currently in development and
        presentations of my research.
      </p>
    </section>


    <!-- Publications -->
    <section class="publication-section">
      <div class="section-heading">
        <h2>Manuscripts in Preparation</h2>

        <p>
          The following projects are currently being developed under the
          mentorship of Dr. Rachel Washburn.
        </p>
      </div>


      <div class="publication-list">

        <article class="publication-item">
          <span class="status-tag">In Preparation</span>

          <h3>
            Appalachian Microbial Communities: Geological Influences and
            Knowledge Gaps
          </h3>

          <p class="citation">
            Apostolides, V., and Washburn, R.
          </p>

          <p>
            A literature review examining microbial communities across the
            Appalachian Mountains and how the region's diverse geology,
            topography, and environmental conditions may contribute to
            microbial diversity.
          </p>
        </article>


        <article class="publication-item">
          <span class="status-tag">In Preparation</span>

          <h3>
            Human and Biological Impacts on Karst Systems: Emerging
            Microbial Knowledge Gaps
          </h3>

          <p class="citation">
            Apostolides, V., and Washburn, R.
          </p>

          <p>
            A literature review investigating how urbanization, agriculture,
            tourism, wildlife, pollution, and microbial communities influence
            karst environments and ecosystem health.
          </p>
        </article>


        <article class="publication-item">
          <span class="status-tag">In Preparation</span>

          <h3>
            Spatial and Temporal Patterns of
            <em>Escherichia coli</em> Across the Kentucky River Basin
          </h3>

          <p class="citation">
            Apostolides, V., Washburn, R., et al.
          </p>

          <p>
            An analysis of long-term citizen-science monitoring data from
            Watershed Watch in Kentucky examining relationships among
            <em>E. coli</em>, rainfall, turbidity, location, and seasonality
            across the Kentucky River Basin.
          </p>
        </article>

      </div>
    </section>


    <!-- Presentations -->
